 "verification_notes": [
  "All private source and detailed sidecars agree at 1/16 threads. The final binary also agrees byte-for-byte with the preceding fully parser-audited private artifact; private-bridge records both executable identities. Reused private parser and changed-file compilation reports are bound to those identical source/sidecar hashes.",
  "The source-known study was unblinded after the first binary recovered no positive O2 helper sites. Initial source-call precision/recall is 0/0 percent (two handwritten false positives). Later 60/37.5 percent figures describe development regression, not independent holdout accuracy.",
  "The baseline fails the new captured-cell observation at all three g1 optimization profiles; all six revised profiles pass. Some prior private reconstructed calls expand because reference-captured eager arguments are now refused independently of SSA assumptions.",
  "Four prior conditional runtime dataflow results change from proved to different after exact guard refinement. Finite VM agreement does not promote those classifications. All public dataflow statuses are unchanged; 45 public holdout source hashes are unchanged.",
  "The final small fix excludes unused-parameter arithmetic patterns that cannot reconstruct any complete argument list. Such patterns no longer veto opt-in loop synthesis. Only the unit-stride study family synthesizes a loop at O2/g1,g2; default remains off.",
  "A full-disk event interrupted preliminary exports and audits. Their incomplete reports were not accepted. Failed exports and audits were rerun after cleaning Cargo caches and compressing generated output. Export timings overlap validation/compression and are not R7 performance evidence.",
  "R9 remains paused; AI is disabled by default. No model execution/download or model/binary/compiler-profile/private-source/bytecode publication. Selected source galleries contain only the authored study fixtures.",
  "Five archived JSON reports use an LF whitespace projection; their parsed fields are unchanged. Source/output galleries and their locked byte hashes are preserved exactly."
